AWK(1)                      User Commands                    AWK(1)

NAME
    awk - pattern scanning and processing language

SYNOPSIS
    awk [-F fs] [-v var=value] [-safe] program [file...]
    awk [-F fs] [-v var=value] [-safe] -f program_file [file...]

DESCRIPTION
    awk reads each input record, splits it into fields and runs the actions
    of the program whose patterns match it. Without files it reads standard
    input. The language is the one of POSIX and of the book The AWK
    Programming Language.

OPTIONS
    -F fs          set the field separator
    -v var=value   assign a variable before BEGIN runs
    -f file        read the program from file; may be repeated
    -safe          disable file output, pipes and system
    --version      print the release

LANGUAGE
    BEGIN, END, /regex/, relational and range patterns; if, while, do, for,
    for (key in array), break, continue, next, exit, return; user defined
    functions; associative arrays with delete and in; printf; getline in
    its forms; output to files and pipes with close and fflush; system.

    Built-in variables: NR NF FS OFS RS ORS FILENAME FNR SUBSEP RSTART
    RLENGTH ENVIRON ARGC ARGV.
    String functions: length substr index split sub gsub match sprintf
    tolower toupper. Strings are UTF-8; length and substr count characters.
    Arithmetic functions: int sqrt exp log sin cos atan2 rand srand.
    Time functions: systime strftime mktime.

EXAMPLES
    awk '{ print $1 }' file
    awk -F: '$3 > 100 { n++ } END { print n }' /etc/passwd

SEE ALSO
    sed(1), grep(1), sh(1)
